"Why?" Ayla asked the Tree. "Why does the sun rise? Why do rivers flow? Why do I feel this ache to understand?"

The Tree shuddered, for no one had ever asked it anything. From its branches fell a single golden fruit. When Ayla ate it, a fire ignited in her mind—the spark of curiosity.

