But others resented the gift. They remembered the old stories of contentment and grew bitter. "Ayla has cursed us," they said. "We can never rest. We can never simply be."

One day, Ayla's great-granddaughter Mira returned to the Tree of Knowing. "The people suffer," she said. "Some wish to return the gift. Can you take it back?"

The Tree rustled its leaves thoughtfully. "I cannot," it said. "But I can offer wisdom: curiosity is not a curse unless you make it so. Ask questions, but also rest in wonder. Seek answers, but also sit in mystery. The contentment you lost was ignorance. The contentment you can gain is acceptance."

